describes the desktop design.

15
00:00:48,520 --> 00:00:52,060
The model can also return
included or needs clarification.

16
00:00:53,200 --> 00:00:54,860
It suggests a rate card item.

17
00:00:55,300 --> 00:00:58,560
The designer remains responsible
for the deliverables and price.

18
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:01,280
The designer reviews
the mobile deliverable

19
00:01:01,280 --> 00:01:04,720
and confirms the $250 rate card price.

20
00:01:05,420 --> 00:01:08,420
The client gets a separate
page for that exact revision.

21
00:01:09,120 --> 00:01:12,420
Approval requires explicit
consent to the deliverables,

22
00:01:12,720 --> 00:01:15,120
total, and payment before work term.

23
00:01:15,860 --> 00:01:17,980
The approval transition is condensed here.

24
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:23,660
Only after approval does the backend
create the PayPal sandbox invoice.

25
00:01:24,560 --> 00:01:26,600
Approval itself is not payment.

26
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:30,300
This is the actual PayPal
invoice for the same change.

27
00:01:31,117 --> 00:01:33,322
If preparation is interrupted, recovery

28
00:01:33,322 --> 00:01:36,485
